{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration observed the proposed difference: early `Advance` let the node become a candidate using old membership; applying self-removal first kept it a follower. That rules out serialization as a protection, but does not settle whether delaying the callback is permitted.\n\nI also found a separate read-authority question: the singleton read shortcut checks voter count, while leader removal need not force step-down. I’ll retain that lead and pause the ambiguous early-`Advance` Candidate.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));q=r['candidates'][0]['question'];cid=r['candidates'][0]['id'];q['unknowns']=['Whether delaying ApplyConfChange until after early Node.Advance is permitted for a committed configuration entry; interface and package guidance need reconciliation.','Whether an applicable no-campaign obligation is stronger than the accounted-frontier guard and can be grounded without assuming actual configuration installation.'];q['counterevidence']=[x for x in q['counterevidence'] if not x.startswith('No legal stale-configuration')];q['counterevidence']+=['Exploration e334066fc8334a10b647e3ad10a35d36 used a declared restart image, not executed quorum commitment history; it observed candidacy only, without election victory or a safety endpoint.','README and raft.proto specify configuration effectiveness at application, so committed self-removal alone cannot be treated as already-effective removal.'];q['trigger_rationale']='Public Node exploration excludes serialization as the missing protection: early Advance advances applied to 2 while retaining node 2 as voter, then Campaign enters StateCandidate at term 2; callback-before-Advance remains StateFollower at term 1. Further variants cannot resolve the remaining normative ordering ambiguity, so pause this question and investigate the independently sourced singleton read-authority premise.'\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'));m['version']=2\nb=next(x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='b-read');b['important_branches'][0]='Non-singleton leader postpones requests until an entry is committed in its term. The singleton shortcut checks only that incoming voter count is one and outgoing count is zero, then returns the local committed index; it does not itself verify that the sole voter is the requesting leader.';b['source_ids']+=['s-singleton-predicate','s-removal-option']